<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
    The motion layer's resource half: the lift shadow's values, and the override that stops the stock
    template painting every shadow white. The curves, durations and the behaviours that run them are
    in Services/Motion.

    Merged LAST, after AppStyles.xaml, for one reason: the implicit Shadow style below has to outrank
    the template's, and resource lookup finds exactly one implicit style per type, taking it from the
    last dictionary merged.

    As in Colors.xaml and Brushes.xaml, CSS custom properties are named without their leading double
    hyphen, because XML forbids a doubled hyphen inside a comment.
-->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml">

    <!-- ===================================================================================
         LIFT SHADOW  (app.css token: shadow-lift)

         CardLift reads these four keys and builds the shadow from them, so the lift is retuned here
         rather than in code.

         The web stacks three layers: a 1px light top edge, a wide dark drop, and a warm brand-tinted
         bloom beneath it. MAUI paints exactly one shadow per element, so only the dark drop is
         ported. The two that are lost are the ones that read as "lit", which is why the mobile card
         reads as raised rather than as picked out by a light — the approximation Requirement 6.5
         asks to be recorded.

         Colour and alpha are separated: Android composites the shadow through its own paint, so a
         brush that already carries alpha is multiplied twice and comes out far too faint.
         =================================================================================== -->

    <!-- shadow-lift layer 2, dark theme: rgba(0, 0, 0, .92) -->
    <Color x:Key="ShadowLift">#000000</Color>
    <x:Double x:Key="ShadowLiftOpacity">0.92</x:Double>

    <!-- shadow-lift layer 2, light theme: rgba(16, 24, 40, .34). Blue-black rather than black, and
         at barely a third the strength: on a bone page a true black drop reads as dirt. -->
    <Color x:Key="ShadowLiftLight">#101828</Color>
    <x:Double x:Key="ShadowLiftOpacityLight">0.34</x:Double>

    <!-- ===================================================================================
         IMPLICIT SHADOW STYLE

         The stock template declares an implicit Shadow style whose brush is White in BOTH themes.
         Against the charcoal ramp that renders as a pale halo rather than a shadow, and because it
         is implicit it would reach the lift shadow too. Overridden here rather than by editing
         Styles.xaml, which stays untouched so a MAUI template update does not have to be re-merged
         by hand.

         Every setter the template had is carried, because an implicit style replaces the template's
         outright rather than layering over it — the values are retuned, not dropped. Offset goes to
         a straight-down drop: the template's diagonal 10,10 belongs to a design with a light source
         off to one side, and neither the storefront nor this app has one.
         =================================================================================== -->

    <Style TargetType="Shadow">
        <Setter Property="Radius" Value="15" />
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.5" />
        <Setter Property="Brush"
                Value="{AppThemeBinding Light={StaticResource ShadowLiftLight}, Dark={StaticResource ShadowLift}}" />
        <Setter Property="Offset" Value="0,6" />
    </Style>

</ResourceDictionary>
